@@ -21,0 +22,2 @@ The technical distinctions returned by [[A33-Epistemic-Cultivation-Operational-P
+The middle term in the inherited arrow is **mind in its mediating office**, not Mind as the exhaustive name of reality. The accepted whole is Life / Mind: Subjective Immediacy is pramātṛ, Objective Internality is pramāṇa, and World is prameya. The arrow therefore reads Subject / Consciousness → the constituted means of appearing → determinate object **within this whole**, while preserving its positive ontological dependence. It does not place Life after Subject as a separately manufactured substance or identify Life with an inspectable state-space. [A/C](../conjugate/AC.md) recovers this relation through the full recognition-matheme; [C41](../concepts/C41-Objective-Internality.md) owns the precise definition of the means.
+
